special_abilities:
  - name: "The P.P.E. Energy Pool"
    description: "Ability 1. A second store of energy inside him that neither he nor anyone else can tap; it is what makes him a Mega-Damage creature and powers his superhuman abilities. Add 4D6 P.P.E. to this pool at every level of experience, starting with level one. When the pool reaches 160 points, or he reaches 15th level, whichever comes first, he dies. He is seriously vulnerable to death from about 12th level."
  - name: "P.P.E. for Spell Casting"
    description: "Ability 2. Base P.P.E. is 1D4x10 plus the P.E. attribute, +2D6 per level; it does not rise when P.E. rises later. He draws double the usual P.P.E. from Songlines/ley lines, and takes the doubled P.P.E. of an animal or person at the moment of death when slain by his own hands, with no blood sacrifice ritual; that energy must be used quickly, but can be held for ten minutes per level of experience. The daily juice does not add to this base."
  - name: "Bonus to Saving Throws"
    description: "Ability 3. +1 to save vs Horror Factor and a flat +1 vs ritual sorcery (both on the sheet)."
  - name: "Sense Ley Line and Magic Energy"
    description: "Ability 4. The same as the Ley Line Walker ability of that name; see the Rifts RPG, page 83."
  - name: "Read Ley Lines"
    description: "Ability 5. The same as the Ley Line Walker ability of that name; see the Rifts RPG, page 83."
  - name: "Spell Knowledge"
    description: "Ability 6. Starts with 10 spells: four 1st level, three 2nd level, two 3rd level and one 4th level. At each further level he can learn one more spell, from the spell level equal to his own level. The knowledge is intuitive, coming to him as it does to a Mystic."
  - name: "Minor Psychic"
    description: "Ability 7. Two Sensitive powers and one Physical power of choice. I.S.P. is the M.E. number +1D6 per level of experience."
  - name: "Songjuice Harvesting"
    description: "Ability 8, a special skill: 35% +4% per level. He detects the trace P.P.E. held by everything along a Songline, gathers the raw material, and meditates on it until it bleeds a pale, sparkling energy that he draws into his body. He must take juice at least once every 24 hours, and by 3rd level it wholly replaces the need or desire for food. Without juice: physical M.D.C., P.P.E. available for spell casting, physical attributes, attacks per melee round and combat bonuses are all halved, and skill performance is -20%."
  - name: "Power and Development: Levels 1-7"
    description: "Ability 9. 1st: +1D6 to P.S., P.E. and P.B., +2D6 to Spd, +3D4x10 physical S.D.C. 2nd: becomes a minor Mega-Damage creature; Hit Points and S.D.C. are replaced by 3D6+12 M.D.C.; +3 initiative, +2 strike, parry and dodge. 3rd: +4D6 M.D.C., +1D6+2 to P.S. and Spd, 1D4 to P.B.; +3 initiative, +2 disarm, +1 parry, +1 dodge. 4th: +2 to save vs all magic, +4 vs possession, +3 spell strength (targets need 15 or higher), -3 to save vs insanity. 5th: +2D6x10+40 M.D.C.; P.S. and P.E. become supernatural; looks no older than 21; leaps 15 feet (4.6 m) high and 20 feet (6 m) across, double with a running start. 6th: running speed doubled, +1 attack per melee round, and a vulnerability (see the next entry). 7th: bio-regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per melee round and regrows a severed limb in 3D4 days; +6 vs possession; -1 to save vs psionic attacks; skill performance -10%."
  - { choose: 1, from: ["Vulnerability (1): Cold/ice", "Vulnerability (2): Fire", "Vulnerability (3-4): Silver", "Vulnerability (5): Wood", "Vulnerability (6): Magic"], note: "Gained at 6th level: roll 1D6 or the G.M. assigns one. Do not apply it before level 6." }
  - name: "Vulnerability (1): Cold/ice"
    description: "From 6th level. M.D. and magical cold or ice do double damage, and S.D.C. versions do their S.D.C. damage as M.D."
  - name: "Vulnerability (2): Fire"
    description: "From 6th level. M.D. and magical fire do double damage, and S.D.C. fire does its S.D.C. damage as M.D."
  - name: "Vulnerability (3-4): Silver"
    description: "From 6th level. M.D. and magical silver weapons do double damage, and S.D.C. silver does its S.D.C. damage as M.D.; a silver dagger that does 1D6 S.D.C. does 1D6 M.D. to him."
  - name: "Vulnerability (5): Wood"
    description: "From 6th level. M.D. and magical wood do double damage, and S.D.C. wooden weapons do their S.D.C. damage as M.D."
  - name: "Vulnerability (6): Magic"
    description: "From 6th level. M.D. and magical attacks of magic do double damage, and S.D.C. versions do their S.D.C. damage as M.D."
  - name: "Power and Development: Levels 8-15"
    description: "Ability 9, the decline. 8th: looks mid-30s with grey in the hair; -1 P.B., -1 to save vs magical attacks. 9th: looks 1D6+4 years older; Spd -1D6+6; physical M.D.C. -3D6. 10th: 1D6+6 years older; -1D4 P.B.; spell strength -3 (targets back to 12 or higher). 11th: 1D6+8 years older; -2 P.B., -2D4 P.S., -6D6 M.D.C.; the extra attack is gone. 12th: 1D6+10 years older; -2 P.B., -1D4 P.S., -6D6 M.D.C.; bio-regeneration is gone, psionic powers are lost, and 1D6 spells are forgotten (player''s choice). 13th: 1D6+12 years older; -3 P.B., -1D4 P.S., -6D6 M.D.C.; speed, combat bonuses and leaping distance are halved; all saving throw bonuses are gone; 1D6+2 skills are forgotten (player''s choice) and all remaining skills are -40%. 14th: 1D6+14 years older; -4 P.B., -1D4 P.S., -6D6 M.D.C.; spell casting P.P.E. is halved and he can no longer draw P.P.E. from ley lines or the slain; all combat bonuses are gone, leaping is impossible, melee attacks and speed are halved again; -40% to save vs coma and death whatever the care. 15th: M.D.C. is reduced to 4D6; remaining spell casting P.P.E. and all attributes are halved; reduced to zero M.D.C. he dies with no save, vanishing in a puff of sparkling blue energy."
  - name: "The Only Hope for Salvation"
    description: "Before 4th level, a willing Songjuicer can be purged by an Aboriginal Shaman in a four hour ritual of dance, song, chant and laying on of hands. He loses all spell casting, every spell he knew and most Songjuicer powers, can never again cast magic or take a magic O.C.C., and starts a new Australian O.C.C. at level one. He keeps 3D6+12 M.D.C., +1D6 M.D.C. per level in the new occupation, +1D6 to P.S., P.E., P.B. and Spd, +1 to save vs disease and poisons and +2 vs possession. The new O.C.C.''s skill bonuses are halved and its O.C.C. bonuses do not apply. From 4th level the progression cannot be stopped."
