extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 81-85 (cache p082-p086, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. The entry heading Songjuicer O.C.C. is on printed 81 below the end of the Sham-Man; printed 82 is an illustration; the nine numbered Songjuicer O.C.C. Bonuses & Abilities are on printed 83-84, with the level table of ability 9 on printed 84 and running onto 85; the stat block, also known as the Power Mage and Fighting Sorcerer, is on printed 85 and ends above Other Possible O.C.C.s. || HEADING: listed under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56; a practitioner of magic, so occ_group is magic. The class prints Base S.D.C. 3D6, stored as sdc_base, so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the Songjuicer ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. It is the class''s own ladder and its bands narrow as the level rises (level 15 begins at 82,201), which the book says is deliberate. || NOT STORED, M.D.C.: the character is an S.D.C. being at level 1 and becomes a Mega-Damage being at level 2 (3D6+12 M.D.C. replacing Hit Points and S.D.C., +4D6 at level 3, +2D6x10+40 at level 5, then -3D6 at 9, -6D6 at each of 11 to 14, and 4D6 flat at 15). No mdc_base is stored because it would make the level-1 character Mega-Damage; the whole M.D.C. ladder is prose in special_abilities and GM Notes. || LEVEL TABLE (ability 9): stored as numbers where the book prints a plain, unconditional number: level 1 +1D6 P.S., P.E. and P.B., +2D6 Spd and +3D4x10 S.D.C. (the text layer prints +3D4xlO) in the bonuses block; level 2 +3 initiative, +2 strike, parry, dodge; level 3 +3 initiative, +2 disarm, +1 parry, +1 dodge; level 4 +2 vs magic (stored as spell and ritual magic), +4 vs possession, -3 vs insanity; level 6 +1 attack; level 7 +6 vs possession (stored as a further 6, as printed) and -1 vs psionics; level 8 -1 vs magical attacks; level 11 the extra attack removed. Kept as prose only: every dice change to an attribute after level 1 (level 3 +1D6+2 P.S. and Spd and 1D4 P.B.; the P.B., P.S. and Spd losses of levels 8-14, including the plain -1 to -4 P.B. figures, kept together with the dice ones rather than half stored); supernatural P.S. and P.E. at level 5; leaping; doubled running speed; bio-regeneration; the skill penalties (-10% at 7, -40% at 13); spell strength +3 at level 4 and back at level 10; the losses of levels 12-15 (psionics, spells and skills forgotten, bonuses halved at 13 and gone at 14, attributes halved at 15), so from level 13 the sheet overstates the stored combat and save bonuses. || VULNERABILITY: the level-6 1D6 table is a pick-one special_abilities group whose option names carry the roll; it is offered at creation and applies from level 6. || ENERGY POOL (ability 1): +4D6 per level from level one, death at 160 points or level 15; prose, not a tracked resource. || P.P.E. (ability 2): 1D4x10 plus P.E. (the text layer prints !D4xlO and calls it Potential Psionic Energy), +2D6 per level. || PSIONICS (ability 7): minor; two Sensitive and one Physical power as two starting groups; I.S.P. is the M.E. number +1D6 per level. They are lost at level 12 (prose). || SPELLS (ability 6): this book prints no spells; the class picks from the general invocations already in the catalog. 10 starting spells as four starting groups (4, 3, 2, 1 of levels 1 to 4) and one spell per level from a level equal to his own as fourteen schedule entries. || SONGJUICE HARVESTING (ability 8): a special skill at 35% +4% per level with no catalog row; kept as a special_abilities entry that carries the percentage. || SKILLS: Speaks English at 92% is stored as Language: Australian English at 92 with the catalog per-level rate. Lore: two of choice is a choice over the catalog Lore rows other than the one the class grants. Hand to Hand: Basic with no alternative is hand_to_hand costs of nothing. || RELATED: Pilot any basic types only, no ''bots, power armor or military vehicles is stored as the Robot Combat rows, Robots & Power Armor and the five Military rows excluded. Cowboy, Electrical, Mechanical, Military and Rogue are printed None and left out. || MONEY: 2D6x200 in cash stored; the further 2D6x200 in tradeable items is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: wristwatch and the clothing accessories have no row; the canteen is printed twice and stored once. The silver dagger, silver cross, notebook and laser distancer use the nearest catalog rows and say so in their notes. Three weapons for each W.P. is the Weapons Matching W.P. Skills row at quantity 3. No vehicle to start."
