## Lore

The Songjuicer is the Outback''s other outsider wizard, and the one the
tribes like least. He treats the magic of the land as fuel. Everything that
lies along a Songline soaks up a trace of its energy, and he has learned to
find those traces, gather them and squeeze them out as a pale, glittering
"juice" that he draws into his own body. Other mages would find the stuff
too thin to notice. He has made himself so sensitive to it that it remakes
him.

At first the result looks like a gift. He grows stronger, faster and better
looking, then tougher than any normal human, and he fights as readily as he
casts spells. But the energy collects in a pool he cannot spend, and the
body was never meant to hold it. After a few years at his peak he begins to
age overnight, his judgement and nerves fray, and the strength drains away
until he dies and scatters as raw energy. A thirty-year-old at the end looks
a hundred.

Songjuicers are driven, restless and dependent on their next harvest; a
shrinking supply makes them fearful and paranoid. Aborigines despise them as
despoilers of the Dreamtime, and settlers are afraid of them. Only an
Aboriginal Shaman can turn one back, and only early on.

## GM Notes

Mega-Damage is not on the sheet. The character is an S.D.C. being at level 1
(3D6 base, +3D4x10). At level 2 Hit Points and S.D.C. are replaced by 3D6+12
M.D.C.; +4D6 at level 3; +2D6x10+40 at level 5; -3D6 at level 9; -6D6 at
each of levels 11, 12, 13 and 14; reduced to 4D6 at level 15. From level 7
to level 11 he regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per melee round.

Energy pool: add 4D6 at every level from level one and keep a running total.
At 160 points, or at 15th level, he dies.

Attribute changes after level 1 are applied by hand: level 3, +1D6+2 P.S.
and Spd, 1D4 P.B.; level 5, P.S. and P.E. become supernatural; level 6,
running speed doubled; level 8, -1 P.B.; level 9, Spd reduced by 1D6+6;
level 10, -1D4 P.B.; level 11, -2 P.B., -2D4 P.S.; level 12, -2 P.B., -1D4
P.S.; level 13, -3 P.B., -1D4 P.S., speed halved; level 14, -4 P.B., -1D4
P.S., speed halved again; level 15, all attributes halved.

The sheet carries the combat and save numbers of levels 2 to 11. It does not
remove them at the end: at level 13 combat bonuses are halved and all save
bonuses are lost, and at level 14 all combat bonuses are gone and attacks
are halved. Spell strength is +3 from level 4 to level 9.

Other losses: skills -10% from level 7 and -40% from level 13; at level 12
the psionic powers go and 1D6 spells are forgotten; at level 13, 1D6+2
skills are forgotten; at level 14 spell casting P.P.E. is halved and no
P.P.E. can be drawn from ley lines or the slain, and saves vs coma and death
are at -40%.

The level-6 vulnerability is picked (or rolled on 1D6) at creation in the
app but does not apply until level 6.

Without Songjuice (at least once every 24 hours): physical M.D.C., spell
casting P.P.E., physical attributes, attacks and combat bonuses are halved
and skills are -20%. Songjuice Harvesting is 35% +4% per level.

The book prints "+6 to save vs possession" at level 7 after "+4" at level 4;
both are stored, for +10 in all. A G.M. who reads the 6 as the new total
should take 4 off.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a wristwatch, clothing
accessories, and two reloads for the sidearm. No vehicle. Money is 2D6x200
in cash plus 2D6x200 in tradeable items. Australian dollars equal credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'songjuicer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'songjuicer';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-songjuicer-class.sql');
